# 伦理学：从法律判决的部分不确定性出发
-在普通法实践中存在大量的‘随机性’因素。我们承认判决结果总体上是有效的，不是因为它们是理想答案，而是一个较为适配各方面需求的解法，即工程解。
-There are lots of so-called 'random' factors in the common law practice. We accept that the judgements are overall acceptable, not because they are ideal answers, but because they represent a solution
that fit demands from various aspects; this means they are solutions based on practical demands, i.e. solution engineered.
-What it has to say with the ethics may cover these threads: 
  -we have reliable reference as to what make sense as an acceptable system
  -but we pronbably have a hard time specifying the nature of ethics, by merely obsereving judgements and the way they work in the world.
